1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:00,520
<u>Testing</u>

2
00:00:01,990 --> 00:00:03,320
<i>What are the main types of tests?</i>

3
00:00:04,570 --> 00:00:08,580
Unit tests check isolated logic, integration tests check several components working together,

4
00:00:08,810 --> 00:00:11,990
and UI tests check the interface and user actions on a device or emulator.

5
00:00:12,690 --> 00:00:17,090
End-to-end tests cover critical flows through the whole application and real or production-like external systems,

6
00:00:17,310 --> 00:00:18,410
so they are used selectively.

7
00:00:19,929 --> 00:00:22,469
<i>How do you make sure a new feature is correct and reduce bugs?</i>

8
00:00:24,003 --> 00:00:28,843
Clarify acceptance criteria and edge cases, design the state and contracts, cover critical logic with tests,

9
00:00:28,973 --> 00:00:29,773
and use code review.

10
00:00:30,483 --> 00:00:35,993
Also verify errors, retries, repeated actions, lifecycle behavior, offline scenarios, and a safe rollout strategy.

11
00:00:37,513 --> 00:00:39,743
<i>How do you go from a feature idea to implementation?</i>

12
00:00:41,251 --> 00:00:47,261
First, clarify the user goal, requirements, and constraints, then design the data flow, UI state, actions, and error handling.

13
00:00:47,971 --> 00:00:52,201
After that, choose a sufficient architecture, split the work into testable steps, write code and tests,

14
00:00:52,351 --> 00:00:55,751
verify scenarios, complete review, and monitor the result after release.

15
00:00:57,617 --> 00:00:58,807
<i>What should be tested first?</i>

16
00:01:00,082 --> 00:01:04,322
Start with business logic, mapping, use cases, reducers, and ViewModel state transitions.

17
00:01:05,012 --> 00:01:08,512
Priority should be based on risk and value rather than trying to cover everything equally.

18
00:01:10,017 --> 00:01:10,967
<i>Mocks or fakes?</i>

19
00:01:12,483 --> 00:01:16,413
Fakes often produce clearer and more stable tests because they provide simple working behavior.

20
00:01:17,123 --> 00:01:20,183
Mocks are useful when a specific interaction really needs to be verified.

21
00:01:21,697 --> 00:01:23,067
<i>How should a ViewModel be tested?</i>

22
00:01:24,590 --> 00:01:27,780
Send input actions and verify observable state transitions and effects.

23
00:01:28,470 --> 00:01:31,480
Test behavior rather than private methods or implementation details.

24
00:01:32,993 --> 00:01:34,813
<i>How should coroutines and Flow be tested?</i>

25
00:01:36,323 --> 00:01:38,713
Use runTest, test dispatchers, and virtual time.

26
00:01:39,423 --> 00:01:42,153
This keeps tests fast and deterministic without Thread.sleep().

27
00:01:43,689 --> 00:01:45,089
<i>Why are UI tests needed?</i>

28
00:01:46,952 --> 00:01:50,382
UI tests verify critical user flows and integration between components.

29
00:01:51,082 --> 00:01:54,792
They are more expensive and fragile than unit tests, so they are usually used selectively.
